#X obj 631 8 conv.degree2key;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 941 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object converts a scale degree to a key number (MIDI
note number in the current octave) \, using the selected scale. A scale
is defined as a sequence of intervals from the tonic \, and the degree
is the index of a step on this scale. The scale can be set with the
SCALE argument or the @scale property. The list of all supported scales
is available in the @all property.;
#X text 240 199 Common Western modes and scales:;
#X text 240 224 'major' — ionian mode. 'minor' — aeolian mode. 'ionian'
\, 'dorian' \, 'phrygian' \, 'lydian' \, 'mixolydian' \, 'aeolian'
\, 'locrian' — the seven modes of the diatonic scale. 'major_pentatonic'
and 'minor_pentatonic' — five-note scales without semitones. 'whole'
— whole-tone scale (six notes \, each a whole step apart). 'whole_leading'
— whole tone plus leading tone (a seven-note symmetric scale). 'chromatic'
— 12-tone chromatic scale. 'chromatic24' — 24-tone microchromatic scale
(quarter tones).;
#X text 240 370 Altered and synthetic Western scales: 'major_harmonic'
\, 'major_melodic' \, 'major_locrian' \, 'major_neapolitan' \, 'minor_harmonic'
\, 'minor_melodic' \, 'minor_melodic_desc' \, 'minor_hungarian' \,
'minor_lydian' \, 'minor_neapolitan' \, 'minor_romanian' \, 'super_locrian'
\, 'augmented' \, 'augmented2' \, 'diminished' \, 'diminished2' \,
'bartok' \, 'hex_aeolian' \, 'hex_dorian' \, 'hex_major6' \, 'hex_major7'
\, 'hex_phrygian' \, 'hex_sus' \, 'prometheus' \, 'scriabin' \, 'ritusen'
— synthetic \, symmetric or altered scales used in classical \, jazz
and contemporary music.;
#X text 240 531 Middle Eastern and Central Asian maqams: 'ahirbhairav'
\, 'ajam' \, 'atharKurd' \, 'bastanikar' \, 'bayati' \, 'farahfaza'
\, 'hijaz' \, 'hijaz_desc' \, 'hijaz_kar' \, 'husseini' \, 'huzam'
\, 'iraq' \, 'jiharkah' \, 'karjighar' \, 'kijaz_kar_kurd' \, 'kurd'
\, 'mahur' \, 'murassah' \, 'mustar' \, 'nahawand' \, 'nahawand_desc'
\, 'nairuz' \, 'nawa_athar' \, 'nikriz' \, 'rast' \, 'rast_desc' \,
'saba' \, 'sikah' \, 'sikah_desc' \, 'suznak' \, 'ushaq_mashri' \,
'yakah' \, 'yakah_desc' \, 'zamzam' \, 'zanjaran' — scales used in
Arabic \, Turkish and Persian music (maqam system).;
#X text 240 692 Indian ragas and Asian scales: 'bhairav' \, 'chinese'
\, 'egyptian' \, 'gong' \, 'hindu' \, 'hirajoshi' \, 'indian' \, 'iwato'
\, 'jiao' \, 'kumoi' \, 'marva' \, 'pelog' \, 'purvi' \, 'shang' \,
'spanish' \, 'todi' \, 'yu' \, 'zhi' — scales from Indian raga tradition
\, Chinese and Japanese (gagaku \, shakuhachi) \, and other Asian musical
systems.;
#X text 240 793 Partch scales: 'partch_o1' ... 'partch_o6' — Harry
Partch's otonalities (major-type just-intonation scales) \, 'partch_u1'
... 'partch_u6' — Partch's utonalities (minor-type just-intonation
scales). These scales are not intended for the 12-tone equal temperament
and sound best when played as just intonation.;
#X text 240 894 Miscellaneous: 'enigmatic' — Verdi's enigmatic scale.
'jiao' — one of the five Chinese pentatonic scales. 'shawq_afza' —
an Arabic maqam with a distinctive augmented-second flavor.;
#X text 240 964 Note: some scales are not intended for the 12-tone
equal temperament.;
